# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use dry-run jobs to get the usage in resource units and service-side validation a job would incur on a real QPU without spending QPU time."
msgstr "Gamitin ang mga dry-run job para makuha ang usage sa resource units at ang service-side validation na maaaring maranasan ng isang job sa totoong QPU nang hindi gumagastos ng QPU time."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs"
msgstr "Mga dry-run job"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs {#dry-run-jobs}"
msgstr "Mga dry-run job {#dry-run-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A dry-run job runs your workload through IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service without using any QPU time. Use a dry-run job to do the following before you commit to a real run:\n"
msgstr "Pinapatakbo ng isang dry-run job ang iyong workload sa IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service nang hindi gumagamit ng anumang QPU time. Gumamit ng dry-run job para gawin ang mga sumusunod bago ka mag-commit sa totoong run:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the usage that the job would incur on the real QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Kunin ang usage na maaaring maranasan ng job sa totoong QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Validate the job.** Quantum Compute checks the job's parameters, the same way it does for a real job.\n"
msgstr "**I-validate ang job.** Sinusuri ng Quantum Compute ang mga parameter ng job, gaya ng ginagawa nito sa totoong job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the [circuit timing schedule](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing)**, if you request it, to debug the job before you run it for real.\n"
msgstr "**Kunin ang [circuit timing schedule](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing)**, kung hihilingin mo ito, para i-debug ang job bago mo ito patakbuhin nang totoo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike dry-run jobs, local testing (fake backends and [Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer)) runs on your own machine and therefore cannot provide usage numbers, service-side validation, or service timing information. To compare the two approaches, see [Mock devices compared to fake backends](#mock-vs-fake).\n"
msgstr "Hindi tulad ng mga dry-run job, ang local testing (mga fake backend at [Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer)) ay tumatakbo sa sarili mong makina kaya hindi ito makapagbibigay ng mga numero ng usage, service-side validation, o impormasyon sa service timing. Para ihambing ang dalawang paraan, tingnan ang [Mock devices kumpara sa mga fake backend](#mock-vs-fake).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"- `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.51.0 or later is required for dry-run jobs.\n"
"- Dry-run jobs are available in all regions, and are only available on the Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans. They are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"- Kinakailangan ang `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.51.0 o mas bago para sa mga dry-run job.\n"
"- Available ang mga dry-run job sa lahat ng rehiyon, at available lang sa mga plan na Flex, Premium, at On-Prem. Hindi sila available sa mga plan na Open o Pay-As-You-Go.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How it works {#how-it-works}"
msgstr "Paano ito gumagana {#how-it-works}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run a dry-run job, pass `dry_run=True` to the primitive's `run()` method:\n"
msgstr "Para magpatakbo ng dry-run job, ipasa ang `dry_run=True` sa `run()` method ng primitive:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`dry_run` is an argument of the `run()` method (the default is `False`), not a runtime option. It is available to all primitives.\n"
msgstr "Ang `dry_run` ay isang argument ng `run()` method (ang default ay `False`), hindi isang runtime option. Available ito sa lahat ng primitive.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A dry-run job has the following characteristics:\n"
msgstr "Ang isang dry-run job ay may mga sumusunod na katangian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "It runs in IBM Quantum Compute Service in the cloud, not on your machine.\n"
msgstr "Tumatakbo ito sa IBM Quantum Compute Service sa cloud, hindi sa iyong makina.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "It uses the calibration data from the real QPU, not just a snapshot. \n"
msgstr "Ginagamit nito ang calibration data mula sa totoong QPU, hindi lang isang snapshot. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its results keep the expected schema and follow the expected shape of results from the real QPU, but contain randomized mock data. They are not actual or simulated measurement results, so do not use them to check physical correctness.\n"
msgstr "Pinananatili ng mga resulta nito ang inaasahang schema at sinusunod ang inaasahang hugis ng mga resulta mula sa totoong QPU, pero naglalaman ng randomized na mock data. Hindi ito totoo o simulated na mga resulta ng pagsukat, kaya huwag itong gamitin para suriin ang pisikal na kawastuhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Processing happens on the server, so the job might not finish immediately.\n"
msgstr "Nangyayari ang pagpoproseso sa server, kaya maaaring hindi agad matapos ang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit size, shots, and other limits are the same as for any job of that program.\n"
msgstr "Ang laki ng circuit, mga shot, at iba pang limitasyon ay kapareho ng sa anumang job ng programang iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`dry_run=True` also works when the backend is already a mock device.\n"
msgstr "Gumagana rin ang `dry_run=True` kapag mock device na ang backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the usage {#read-the-usage}"
msgstr "Basahin ang usage {#read-the-usage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The usage of a completed dry-run job is the usage the same job would incur on the real QPU, except in rare situations where calibration data changes significantly after the dry-run job and before the job on a real QPU.\n"
msgstr "Ang usage ng isang natapos na dry-run job ay ang usage na maaaring maranasan ng parehong job sa totoong QPU, maliban sa mga bihirang sitwasyon kung saan malaki ang pagbabago ng calibration data pagkatapos ng dry-run job at bago ang job sa totoong QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.usage()` returns the usage in seconds.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng `job.usage()` ang usage sa segundo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.metrics()[\"usage\"]` returns the same data together with the usage status.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng `job.metrics()[\"usage\"]` ang parehong data kasama ang usage status.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run usage is not charged, does not consume your plan allocation, and does not count against any limits.\n"
msgstr "Hindi sinisingil ang dry-run usage, hindi ito kumokonsumo ng allocation ng iyong plan, at hindi ito binibilang sa anumang limitasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Do not use job.usage_estimation with dry-run jobs\">\n"
"Do not use `job.usage_estimation` on a dry-run job. Use `job.usage()`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Huwag gamitin ang job.usage_estimation sa mga dry-run job\">\n"
"Huwag gamitin ang `job.usage_estimation` sa isang dry-run job. Gamitin ang `job.usage()`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.usage()` returns `0` until the usage calculation is final, so wait for the job to finish before you read it.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng `job.usage()` ang `0` hanggang sa maging pinal ang pagkalkula ng usage, kaya hintayin munang matapos ang job bago mo ito basahin.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit timing schedule {#circuit-timing-schedule}"
msgstr "Iskedyul ng timing ng circuit {#circuit-timing-schedule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To request the circuit timing schedule, use the same option as for a real job. For full details, see [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"
msgstr "Para hilingin ang circuit timing schedule, gamitin ang parehong option tulad ng sa totoong job. Para sa buong detalye, tingnan ang [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limitations {#limitations}"
msgstr "Mga limitasyon {#limitations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Job and batch modes only.** Dry-run jobs can only run in [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) and [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"
msgstr "**Job at batch mode lang.** Tumatakbo lang ang mga dry-run job sa [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) at [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans only.** Dry-run jobs are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
msgstr "**Mga plan na Flex, Premium, at On-Prem lang.** Hindi available ang mga dry-run job sa mga plan na Open o Pay-As-You-Go.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices {#mock-devices}"
msgstr "Mga mock device {#mock-devices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices are the implementation behind dry-run jobs. Dry-run jobs hide mock devices by default, but you encounter them in these cases:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga mock device ang implementasyon sa likod ng mga dry-run job. Itinatago ng mga dry-run job ang mga mock device bilang default, pero makakaharap mo sila sa mga sumusunod na kaso:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Instances configured to access only mock devices.** Example: if you use `service.backend(\"ibm_phoenix\")` to submit a dry-run job on `ibm_phoenix`, but your instance doesn't have access to `ibm_phoenix`,  you will get a `QiskitBackendNotFoundError`. Instead, select the mock device directly with `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`.\n"
msgstr "**Mga instance na naka-configure para ma-access lang ang mga mock device.** Halimbawa: kung gagamitin mo ang `service.backend(\"ibm_phoenix\")` para magsumite ng dry-run job sa `ibm_phoenix`, pero walang access ang iyong instance sa `ibm_phoenix`, makakakuha ka ng `QiskitBackendNotFoundError`. Sa halip, piliin nang direkta ang mock device gamit ang `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compute resources.** Mock devices are hidden by default on the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page. The table on the page has a filter option to include them, but only the Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans have access to mock devices.\n"
msgstr "**Compute resources.** Nakatago bilang default ang mga mock device sa pahina ng [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers). May filter option ang talahanayan sa pahina para isama sila, pero ang mga plan lang na Flex, Premium, at On-Prem ang may access sa mga mock device.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Workloads table.** Jobs from mock devices are hidden by default on the [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) page. The table has a filter option (the funnel icon) to display them.\n"
msgstr "**Talahanayan ng Workloads.** Nakatago bilang default ang mga job mula sa mga mock device sa pahina ng [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads). May filter option ang talahanayan (ang icon na funnel) para ipakita sila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Python API.** `service.backends()` and `service.jobs()` exclude mock devices unless you call them with `include_mocks=True`. `IBMBackend.is_mock` indicates whether a backend is a mock device. `service.least_busy()` never returns a mock device.\n"
msgstr "**Python API.** Hindi isinasama ng `service.backends()` at `service.jobs()` ang mga mock device maliban kung tatawagin mo sila gamit ang `include_mocks=True`. Ipinapahiwatig ng `IBMBackend.is_mock` kung mock device ang isang backend. Hindi kailanman nagbabalik ng mock device ang `service.least_busy()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"mock-vs-fake\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices compared to fake backends {#mock-devices-compared-to-fake-backends}"
msgstr "Mga mock device kumpara sa mga fake backend {#mock-devices-compared-to-fake-backends}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The names are similar, but a mock device and a [fake backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider) are different things. A fake backend is a local object in your Python environment. A mock device is a cloud resource in IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"
msgstr "Magkahawig ang mga pangalan, pero magkaiba ang mock device at [fake backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider). Ang fake backend ay isang lokal na object sa iyong Python environment. Ang mock device ay isang cloud resource sa IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | Mock device (for example `mock_phoenix`) | Fake backend (for example `FakeManilaV2`) |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| What it is | A device in IBM Quantum Compute Service | A Python class in `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider` |\n"
"| Where it runs | Cloud, in the service | Locally, on your machine |\n"
"| How you get it | `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`, or automatically with `run(..., dry_run=True)` | `from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import ...` |\n"
"| Account and instance | Specific plans only (Flex, Premium, or On-Prem) | All instances and plans |\n"
"| Calibration | Live, matches the real device at any time | Fixed snapshot shipped with the installed package |\n"
"| Results | Randomized data with the expected schema. Not a simulation | Noisy simulation that uses the snapshot's noise model |\n"
"| Physically meaningful results | No. Never use them to check correctness | Approximately, within the limits of the noise model |\n"
"| Usage reported | Yes | None |\n"
"| Charged or counted against plan allocation or limits | No | No |\n"
"| Job validation | Done by the service, same as a real job | Limited to what the client checks |\n"
"| Timing schedule | Available on request  | Not available |\n"
"| Execution modes | Job and batch mode only. Sessions are blocked | Session syntax accepted but ignored (local mode has no real sessions or batches) |\n"
"| Completion | Asynchronous, on the server | Runs locally and returns when finished |\n"
"| Shown in platform interface and API lists | Hidden by default (Compute resources, Workloads table, `backends()`, `jobs()`). Opt in to show | Never, because nothing is sent to the service |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | Mock device (halimbawa `mock_phoenix`) | Fake backend (halimbawa `FakeManilaV2`) |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Ano ito | Isang device sa IBM Quantum Compute Service | Isang Python class sa `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider` |\n"
"| Saan tumatakbo | Cloud, sa service | Lokal, sa iyong makina |\n"
"| Paano ito makukuha | `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`, o awtomatiko gamit ang `run(..., dry_run=True)` | `from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import ...` |\n"
"| Account at instance | Mga partikular na plan lang (Flex, Premium, o On-Prem) | Lahat ng instance at plan |\n"
"| Calibration | Live, tugma sa totoong device anumang oras | Nakapirming snapshot na kasama sa naka-install na package |\n"
"| Mga resulta | Randomized na data na may inaasahang schema. Hindi simulation | Noisy simulation na gumagamit ng noise model ng snapshot |\n"
"| Mga resultang may pisikal na kahulugan | Wala. Huwag kailanman gamitin para suriin ang kawastuhan | Humigit-kumulang, sa loob ng limitasyon ng noise model |\n"
"| May iniuulat na usage | Oo | Wala |\n"
"| Sinisingil o binibilang sa plan allocation o mga limitasyon | Hindi | Hindi |\n"
"| Job validation | Ginagawa ng service, kapareho ng totoong job | Limitado sa sinusuri ng client |\n"
"| Timing schedule | Available kapag hiniling | Hindi available |\n"
"| Mga execution mode | Job at batch mode lang. Naka-block ang mga Session | Tinatanggap ang Session syntax pero binabalewala (walang totoong session o batch ang local mode) |\n"
"| Pagtatapos | Asynchronous, sa server | Lokal na tumatakbo at nagbabalik kapag tapos na |\n"
"| Ipinapakita sa platform interface at mga listahan ng API | Nakatago bilang default (Compute resources, talahanayan ng Workloads, `backends()`, `jobs()`). Mag-opt in para ipakita | Hindi kailanman, dahil walang ipinapadala sa service |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to choose {#how-to-choose}"
msgstr "Paano pumili {#how-to-choose}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find out **how much usage the job will consume, or whether the service will accept it**, use a dry-run job.\n"
msgstr "Para malaman **kung gaano karaming usage ang kokonsumohin ng job, o kung tatanggapin ito ng service**, gumamit ng dry-run job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find out **what the output might look like**, or to work offline, use a fake backend or Aer.\n"
msgstr "Para malaman **kung ano ang maaaring hitsura ng output**, o para magtrabaho offline, gumamit ng fake backend o Aer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To do both, iterate on circuits and results with a fake backend, then dry-run as the last check before the real QPU.\n"
msgstr "Para magawa ang dalawa, mag-iterate sa mga circuit at resulta gamit ang fake backend, pagkatapos mag-dry-run bilang huling pagsusuri bago ang totoong QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common points of confusion {#common-points-of-confusion}"
msgstr "Mga karaniwang kalituhan {#common-points-of-confusion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A mock device is not a simulator.** Its output is random, so sampling a Bell circuit on `mock_phoenix` does not return a Bell distribution. If you want realistic noisy output, use a fake backend.\n"
msgstr "**Ang mock device ay hindi simulator.** Random ang output nito, kaya ang pag-sample ng Bell circuit sa `mock_phoenix` ay hindi nagbabalik ng Bell distribution. Kung gusto mo ng makatotohanang noisy na output, gumamit ng fake backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A fake backend is not the live device.** Its calibration is a snapshot and might be out of date. A mock device tracks the real calibration, so transpiled circuits and timing match what the QPU sees today.\n"
msgstr "**Ang fake backend ay hindi ang live na device.** Snapshot ang calibration nito at maaaring luma na. Sinusubaybayan ng mock device ang totoong calibration, kaya tugma ang mga transpiled na circuit at timing sa nakikita ng QPU ngayon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Neither runs on real hardware.** Neither consumes QPU time, but only a dry-run job goes through the service.\n"
msgstr "**Wala sa dalawa ang tumatakbo sa totoong hardware.** Wala sa dalawa ang kumokonsumo ng QPU time, pero dry-run job lang ang dumadaan sa service.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`usage_estimation` is not the dry-run estimate.** For a dry-run job, `job.usage()` returns the seconds of usage your job would be charged on a real QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Ang `usage_estimation` ay hindi ang dry-run estimate.** Para sa dry-run job, ibinabalik ng `job.usage()` ang mga segundo ng usage na sisingilin sa iyong job sa totoong QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use cases {#use-cases}"
msgstr "Mga use case {#use-cases}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Students and courses {#students-and-courses}"
msgstr "Mga estudyante at kurso {#students-and-courses}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An administrator restricts an instance to mock devices only, using the QPU customization toggle when [creating or editing the instance](/guides/instances#add-instance). Students then validate their payloads end-to-end without consuming real QPU time or RUs. Because the instance has access only to mock devices, students select the backend by its mock name:\n"
msgstr "Nililimitahan ng isang administrator ang isang instance sa mga mock device lang, gamit ang QPU customization toggle kapag [gumagawa o nag-e-edit ng instance](/guides/instances#add-instance). Pagkatapos ay maaaring i-validate ng mga estudyante ang kanilang mga payload nang end-to-end nang hindi kumokonsumo ng totoong QPU time o RU. Dahil mock device lang ang may access ang instance, pinipili ng mga estudyante ang backend gamit ang mock name nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Project planning {#project-planning}"
msgstr "Pagpaplano ng proyekto {#project-planning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A team about to start a project dry-runs representative jobs to see the RUs the project needs, before choosing a plan or allocation:\n"
msgstr "Ang isang team na malapit nang magsimula ng proyekto ay nagdadry-run ng mga kinatawang job para makita ang mga RU na kailangan ng proyekto, bago pumili ng plan o allocation:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Final check before running on a real QPU {#final-check-before-running-on-a-real-qpu}"
msgstr "Huling pagsusuri bago tumakbo sa totoong QPU {#final-check-before-running-on-a-real-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Validate parameters and inspect the timing schedule with `dry_run=True`, then drop the argument and run on the real QPU. Nothing else in your code changes:\n"
msgstr "I-validate ang mga parameter at suriin ang timing schedule gamit ang `dry_run=True`, pagkatapos alisin ang argument at patakbuhin sa totoong QPU. Walang ibang magbabago sa iyong code:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- Test programs on your own machine with [Local testing mode](/guides/local-testing-mode).\n"
